---
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro';
import Link from '../components/Link.astro';
import { routes } from '../data/site';
---

<TextPage
  title="About PartyPrintKit"
  description="Who makes PartyPrintKit, why every kit ships as one coordinated PDF, and what free actually means here: no editor, no account and no watermark."
  path="/about/"
  crumb="About"
  eyebrow="About"
  heading="About PartyPrintKit."
  lede="Free printable party decorations that already belong together, made to print on the paper you have at home."
>
  <h2>Why a kit and not a template</h2>
  <p>
    Most free party printables are single files from unrelated sources: a banner in one style, hats
    in another, toppers in a third. They print fine and look like three different parties on one
    table. Everything here is drawn as a set, so the banner, hats, toppers, signs and tags share a
    palette, a shape language and a cut line.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no editor, no account and no watermark. You download a PDF, print it and cut it out.
  </p>

  <h2>Made for a real printer</h2>
  <p>
    Every sheet is designed against the constraints of a home inkjet: no full-page colour fills,
    nothing thinner than half a point, true A4 and US Letter files instead of one file scaled to
    fit. The reasoning behind each of those choices is in the{' '}
    <Link route={routes.printingGuide} class="text-link" label="printing guide" />.
  </p>

  <h2>Who makes it</h2>
  <p>
    PartyPrintKit is a small independent project, not a marketplace and not a template farm. Every
    kit is drawn, printed and assembled before it is published, and the photographs on the site are
    of the actual printed pieces.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Requests for an occasion, a design or a piece that is missing are welcome, and so are reports of
    anything that prints wrong. Write to <a href="mailto:info@partyprintkit.com">info@partyprintkit.com</a>
    or use the <Link route={routes.contact} class="text-link" label="contact page" />.
  </p>
</TextPage>
